    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d975c25d-18dc-5d94-836a-5309bf4a36ec",
      ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n-30^\\circ=210^\\circ-240^\\circ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(-30^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(-30^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-30^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(210^\\circ-240^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(210^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(240^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(210^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(240^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
