      ":question/id": "9412543e-8478-5a91-9622-0817e2102b45",
      ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n345^\\circ=45^\\circ+300^\\circ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(345^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(345^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x+y)=\\cos x\\cos y-\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(345^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(45^\\circ+300^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(300^\\circ\\right)-\\sin\\left(45^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(300^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}-\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
